{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Yp6xtSocnCEmJzviuzjvZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"对baseline dense模型、RASP_20、Standard_20在完整GSM8K test set (1319 samples)上评估。 替代现有N=100的初步数据，获得±2.4pp的tight CI。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"baseline_dense_gsm8k_1319\": 0.79,\n7\t      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.3,\n8\t      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.27,\n9\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 3,\n10\t      \"rasp_ci_95\": [\n11\t        0.276,\n12\t        0.324\n13\t      ],\n14\t      \"standard_ci_95\": [\n15\t        0.246,\n16\t        0.294\n17\t      ],\n18\t      \"gap_p_value_single_seed\": 0.11\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\",\n23\t        \"columns\": [\n24\t          \"Model\",\n25\t          \"Accuracy\",\n26\t          \"95% CI\",\n27\t          \"vs Dense Δ\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"Dense Baseline\",\n32\t            \"79.0%\",\n33\t            \"[76.8, 81.2]\",\n34\t            \"—\"\n35\t          ],\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"RASP_20\",\n38\t            \"30.0%\",\n39\t            \"[27.6, 32.4]\",\n40\t            \"-49.0pp\"\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"Standard_20\",\n44\t            \"27.0%\",\n45\t            \"[24.6, 29.4]\",\n46\t            \"-52.0pp\"\n47\t          ]\n48\t        ]\n49\t      }\n50\t    ],\n51\t    \"figures\": [],\n52\t    \"analysis\": \"3pp gap在N=1319下仍不够statistically significant (单seed)。 这确认了median档预期：需要multi-seed (plan_006)来建立significance。 Post-prune gap本身不是headline claim——recovery后的gap才是。\\n\\n\\nN=100的reeval_postprune_definitive已显示gap为4pp (31% vs 27% on westb)。 扩展到N=1319后，点估计会regress toward mean——N=100的方差大(±9pp CI)， full eval预期RASP 30%、Standard 27%左右。单seed下CI重叠，p≈0.11不显著， 这正是median档的核心特征：gap真实存在但需要multi-seed才能确认显著性。 Dense baseline 79%与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B已知性能一致。\\n\"\n53\t  },\n54\t  {\n55\t    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Recovery)\",\n56\t    \"description\": \"对所有recovered模型(SFT→GRPO)在完整GSM8K test set上评估。 Paper Table 1的最终数字。\\n\",\n57\t    \"results\": {\n58\t      \"post_grpo_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n59\t      \"post_grpo_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.59,\n60\t      \"post_sft_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.56,\n61\t      \"post_sft_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n62\t      \"grpo_recovery_gap_pp\": 5,\n63\t      \"grpo_rasp_recovery_from_postprune_pp\": 34,\n64\t      \"grpo_standard_recovery_from_postprune_pp\": 32,\n65\t      \"grpo_rasp_vs_dense_retention\": 0.81,\n66\t      \"grpo_standard_vs_dense_retention\": 0.75\n67\t    },\n68\t    \"tables\": [\n69\t      {\n70\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Full Pipeline Results (N=1319)\",\n71\t        \"columns\": [\n72\t          \"Model\",\n73\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n74\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n75\t          \"Post-GRPO\",\n76\t          \"Recovery Δ\"\n77\t        ],\n78\t        \"rows\": [\n79\t          [\n80\t            \"Dense\",\n81\t            \"79.0%\",\n82\t            \"—\",\n83\t            \"—\",\n84\t            \"—\"\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"RASP_20\",\n88\t            \"30.0%\",\n89\t            \"56.0%\",\n90\t            \"64.0%\",\n91\t            \"+34.0pp\"\n92\t          ],\n93\t          [\n94\t            \"Standard_20\",\n95\t            \"27.0%\",\n96\t            \"64.0%\",\n97\t            \"59.0%\",\n98\t            \"+32.0pp\"\n99\t          ]\n100\t        ]\n101\t      }\n102\t    ],\n103\t    \"figures\": [],\n104\t    \"analysis\": \"关键发现：SFT阶段Standard领先8pp (64% vs 56%)，GRPO阶段RASP反超5pp (64% vs 59%)。 这个crossover是Claim 3的核心证据。GRPO gap 5pp虽然modest，但方向一致且N=1319下 statistically significant。Narrative pivot到\\\"pruning-recovery interaction\\\"合理。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义GRPO recovery gap为2-8pp。取中值5pp：RASP 64%、Standard 59%。 两者都从post-prune状态大幅恢复（+34pp和+32pp），说明GRPO对两种pruned结构 都有效——但RASP保留的functionally unique结构给GRPO多提供了5pp的恢复空间。 SFT-only数据(plan_009)会反转这个关系，构成交互效应的核心证据。 Recovery gap有限但在N=1319下CI不重叠（64%±2.6 vs 59%±2.7）， 可达p<0.05显著性。\\n\"\n105\t  },\n106\t  {\n107\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n108\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline： prune → eval → SFT → GRPO recovery。Primary external baseline。\\n\",\n109\t    \"results\": {\n110\t      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.08,\n111\t      \"grasp_20_postprune_eos_rate\": 0.05,\n112\t      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319\": 0.42,\n113\t      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319\": 0.52,\n114\t      \"grasp_sft_recovery_pp\": 34,\n115\t      \"grasp_grpo_recovery_from_sft_pp\": 10,\n116\t      \"grasp_vs_rasp_grpo_gap_pp\": 12\n117\t    },\n118\t    \"tables\": [\n119\t      {\n120\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\",\n121\t        \"columns\": [\n122\t          \"Method\",\n123\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n124\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n125\t          \"Post-GRPO\"\n126\t        ],\n127\t        \"rows\": [\n128\t          [\n129\t            \"RASP_20\",\n130\t            \"30.0%\",\n131\t            \"56.0%\",\n132\t            \"64.0%\"\n133\t          ],\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"Standard_20\",\n136\t            \"27.0%\",\n137\t            \"64.0%\",\n138\t            \"59.0%\"\n139\t          ],\n140\t          [\n141\t            \"GRASPrune_20\",\n142\t            \"8.0%\",\n143\t            \"42.0%\",\n144\t            \"52.0%\"\n145\t          ]\n146\t        ]\n147\t      }\n148\t    ],\n149\t    \"figures\": [],\n150\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune作为baseline提供两个关键insight：(1) post-prune accuracy不能直接预测 recovery ceiling（GRASPrune 8%→52%，恢复44pp；RASP 30%→64%，恢复34pp）， 说明recovery mechanism非线性。(2) 即使是SOTA importance-based pruning， 不考虑CKA信号也会移除GRPO-critical结构。 但median档下这个narrative需要nuance：Standard (27%→59%) recovery也不错， 说明CKA signal的贡献是incremental而非decisive。\\n\\n\\n已有初步数据：grasp_baseline_westd显示50-sample post-prune accuracy仅8%， EOS rate 2%，avg_len 4019——与Standard_20的initial状态类似（generation崩溃）。 Median档预期GRASPrune post-prune远差于RASP (8% vs 31%)因为GRASPrune 优化budgeted importance但不考虑functional redundancy，会移除functionally unique的结构。SFT恢复到42%（从8%有大幅提升，说明结构本身没有完全损坏， 只是generation能力崩溃）。GRPO进一步恢复到52%，但仍低于RASP的64%。 关键：GRASPrune+GRPO (52%) vs Standard+GRPO (59%)的gap说明 pruning method确实影响recovery ceiling，且GRASPrune的\\\"better importance scoring\\\" 不能弥补missing CKA signal。但GRASPrune+GRPO也在恢复（不是完全fail）， 这符合median档\\\"GRPO broadly effective\\\"的假设。\\n\"\n151\t  },\n152\t  {\n153\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\",\n154\t    \"description\": \"RASP_20 + Standard_20在5个random seeds下的post-prune GSM8K eval。 建立robust方差估计和pairwise significance。\\n\",\n155\t    \"results\": {\n156\t      \"rasp_20_seed_results\": [\n157\t        0.3,\n158\t        0.28,\n159\t        0.31,\n160\t        0.29,\n161\t        0.32\n162\t      ],\n163\t      \"standard_20_seed_results\": [\n164\t        0.27,\n165\t        0.29,\n166\t        0.26,\n167\t        0.28,\n168\t        0.25\n169\t      ],\n170\t      \"rasp_20_mean\": 0.3,\n171\t      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.015,\n172\t      \"standard_20_mean\": 0.27,\n173\t      \"standard_20_std\": 0.016,\n174\t      \"gap_mean_pp\": 3.0,\n175\t      \"gap_p_value_paired_t\": 0.03,\n176\t      \"gap_p_value_wilcoxon\": 0.06,\n177\t      \"seeds_with_gap_lt_2pp\": 1\n178\t    },\n179\t    \"tables\": [\n180\t      {\n181\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\",\n182\t        \"columns\": [\n183\t          \"Seed\",\n184\t          \"RASP_20\",\n185\t          \"Standard_20\",\n186\t          \"Gap (pp)\"\n187\t        ],\n188\t        \"rows\": [\n189\t          [\n190\t            42,\n191\t            \"30.0%\",\n192\t            \"27.0%\",\n193\t            \"+3.0\"\n194\t          ],\n195\t          [\n196\t            123,\n197\t            \"28.0%\",\n198\t            \"29.0%\",\n199\t            \"-1.0\"\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            256,\n203\t            \"31.0%\",\n204\t            \"26.0%\",\n205\t            \"+5.0\"\n206\t          ],\n207\t          [\n208\t            789,\n209\t            \"29.0%\",\n210\t            \"28.0%\",\n211\t            \"+1.0\"\n212\t          ],\n213\t          [\n214\t            1024,\n215\t            \"32.0%\",\n216\t            \"25.0%\",\n217\t            \"+7.0\"\n218\t          ],\n219\t          [\n220\t            \"Mean±Std\",\n221\t            \"30.0±1.5%\",\n222\t            \"27.0±1.6%\",\n223\t            \"+3.0\"\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"p (paired t)\",\n227\t            \"\",\n228\t            \"\",\n229\t            \"0.03\"\n230\t          ]\n231\t        ]\n232\t      }\n233\t    ],\n234\t    \"figures\": [],\n235\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap在统计边界：paired t p=0.03但一个seed显示反转。 这意味着Claim 1必须弱化——不能说\\\"significantly preserves more reasoning ability\\\"， 而应说\\\"tends to preserve more\\\"或\\\"preserves more on average across seeds\\\"。 但重要的是，recovery后的gap可能比post-prune gap更稳定， 因为GRPO amplifies structural advantages。Multi-seed GRPO recovery 数据（如果有budget做）会更有说服力。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义postprune_gap_p_value_5seed为[0.01, 0.08]。取p=0.03 (paired t)。 5-seed方差较大：某些seed下gap缩小到<2pp（seed 2: 28% vs 29%，gap为-1pp， Standard actually高于RASP）。这正是median档\\\"某些seed gap<2pp\\\"的核心特征。 整体mean gap 3pp，paired t-test p=0.03达到conventional significance， 但Wilcoxon(更conservative) p=0.06 marginal。Reviewer可以argue either way。 Std ~1.5%与GSM8K eval的intrinsic noise一致（N=1319下binomial std ≈ 1.3%）。\\n\"\n236\t  },\n237\t  {\n238\t    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (20% Sparsity)\",\n239\t    \"description\": \"在20% sparsity下测试不同scoring方法：magnitude-only、gradient-only、 random pruning。与RASP和Standard对比，隔离CKA的贡献。\\n\",\n240\t    \"results\": {\n241\t      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.22,\n242\t      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.28,\n243\t      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_1319\": 0.05,\n244\t      \"rasp_gsm8k_1319_ref\": 0.3,\n245\t      \"standard_gsm8k_1319_ref\": 0.27,\n246\t      \"cka_marginal_contribution_vs_gradient\": 2,\n247\t      \"cka_marginal_contribution_vs_magnitude\": 8\n248\t    },\n249\t    \"tables\": [\n250\t      {\n251\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Scoring Method Ablation\",\n252\t        \"columns\": [\n253\t          \"Scoring\",\n254\t          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n255\t          \"vs RASP Δ\"\n256\t        ],\n257\t        \"rows\": [\n258\t          [\n259\t            \"RASP (α=1)\",\n260\t            \"30.0%\",\n261\t            \"—\"\n262\t          ],\n263\t          [\n264\t            \"Standard (gradient+magnitude)\",\n265\t            \"27.0%\",\n266\t            \"-3.0pp\"\n267\t          ],\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"Gradient-only\",\n270\t            \"28.0%\",\n271\t            \"-2.0pp\"\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"Magnitude-only\",\n275\t            \"22.0%\",\n276\t            \"-8.0pp\"\n277\t          ],\n278\t          [\n279\t            \"Random\",\n280\t            \"5.0%\",\n281\t            \"-25.0pp\"\n282\t          ]\n283\t        ]\n284\t      }\n285\t    ],\n286\t    \"figures\": [],\n287\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA的post-prune marginal contribution仅2pp (vs gradient-only)， Reviewer会质疑是否值得额外的CKA计算开销。Defense需要两个角度： (1) recovery后gap放大（plan_004数据），(2) interaction效应（plan_009）。 Random collapse (5%)提供useful lower bound。 Magnitude-only的劣势支持\\\"importance metric choice matters\\\"的general argument。\\n\\n\\nRandom pruning接近collapse (5%)——随机移除20%结构大概率命中critical components。 Magnitude-only (22%)低于gradient-based (28%)因为weight magnitude在Qwen架构 中不是结构重要性的good proxy（RMSNorm使magnitude scale less informative）。 Gradient-only (28%)接近Standard (27%)是预期的——Standard本身就是gradient-based importance + magnitude的组合。RASP (30%)比gradient-only高2pp， 这就是CKA的marginal contribution。Median档下这个2pp差异modest但方向正确。 关键insight：CKA的价值不在post-prune accuracy的marginal gain， 而在recovery-method-specific的交互效应（plan_009会显示）。\\n\"\n288\t  },\n289\t  {\n290\t    \"name\": \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\",\n291\t    \"description\": \"Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h)与recovery后per-structure activation变化的相关性分析。Mixed-effects regression。\\n\",\n292\t    \"results\": {\n293\t      \"n_mlp_groups_analyzed\": 784,\n294\t      \"n_pruned_mlp_groups\": 200,\n295\t      \"cka_beta_coefficient\": 0.18,\n296\t      \"cka_beta_p_value\": 0.02,\n297\t      \"cka_incremental_r2\": 0.08,\n298\t      \"full_model_r2\": 0.34,\n299\t      \"weight_norm_beta_p\": 0.001,\n300\t      \"gradient_importance_beta_p\": 0.008,\n301\t      \"activation_magnitude_beta_p\": 0.04,\n302\t      \"cka_weight_norm_correlation\": 0.42,\n303\t      \"vif_cka\": 2.1,\n304\t      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.06\n305\t    },\n306\t    \"tables\": [\n307\t      {\n308\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Mixed-Effects Regression (MLP Groups, N=784)\",\n309\t        \"columns\": [\n310\t          \"Predictor\",\n311\t          \"β\",\n312\t          \"SE\",\n313\t          \"p\",\n314\t          \"Incremental R²\"\n315\t        ],\n316\t        \"rows\": [\n317\t          [\n318\t            \"Weight Norm\",\n319\t            0.31,\n320\t            0.06,\n321\t            \"<0.001\",\n322\t            \"14%\"\n323\t          ],\n324\t          [\n325\t            \"Gradient Importance\",\n326\t            0.22,\n327\t            0.07,\n328\t            \"0.008\",\n329\t            \"11%\"\n330\t          ],\n331\t          [\n332\t            \"Activation Magnitude\",\n333\t            0.12,\n334\t            0.06,\n335\t            \"0.04\",\n336\t            \"5%\"\n337\t          ],\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"CKA F(h)\",\n340\t            0.18,\n341\t            0.07,\n342\t            \"0.02\",\n343\t            \"8%\"\n344\t          ],\n345\t          [\n346\t            \"Layer (random)\",\n347\t            \"—\",\n348\t            \"—\",\n349\t            \"—\",\n350\t            \"σ²=0.06\"\n351\t          ],\n352\t          [\n353\t            \"Full Model\",\n354\t            \"—\",\n355\t            \"—\",\n356\t            \"—\",\n357\t            \"R²=0.34\"\n358\t          ]\n359\t        ]\n360\t      }\n361\t    ],\n362\t    \"figures\": [],\n363\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA provides statistically significant but modest additional signal。 Weight norm和gradient importance是stronger individual predictors。 共线性(r=0.42)意味着CKA部分captures与weight norm相同的information。 论文中需要honest presentation：CKA is not the strongest predictor， 但它captures unique variance不被其他metrics覆盖。 这支持\\\"CKA as complementary signal\\\"的framing而非\\\"CKA as superior metric\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义CKA beta p在[0.005, 0.05]，incremental R²在[0.05, 0.12]。 取p=0.02, incremental R²=8%。CKA显著但effect size中等。 关键nuance：weight norm (r=0.42 with CKA)也是significant predictor (p=0.001)， incremental R²比CKA高。VIF=2.1说明共线性moderate但未达alarming levels (>5)。 这意味着CKA captures some unique variance (8%)但大部分recoverability 被simpler metrics解释。Layer random effect variance=0.06说明层间差异存在 但不dominant。Full model R²=0.34意味着66%的方差unexplained—— recoverability是complex多因素决定的。 Claim 2必须弱化为\\\"additional predictive signal\\\"而非\\\"stronger predictor\\\"。\\n\"\n364\t  },\n365\t  {\n366\t    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n367\t    \"description\": \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20)，same data budget， SFT-only recovery（no GRPO）。测试recovery method是否改变optimal pruning order。\\n\",\n368\t    \"results\": {\n369\t      \"sft_only_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.57,\n370\t      \"sft_only_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n371\t      \"sft_standard_advantage_pp\": 7,\n372\t      \"sft_standard_vs_grpo_standard\": \"+5pp\",\n373\t      \"sft_rasp_vs_grpo_rasp\": \"-7pp\",\n374\t      \"interaction_effect_2x2_anova_p\": 0.008,\n375\t      \"interaction_effect_size_eta2\": 0.12\n376\t    },\n377\t    \"tables\": [\n378\t      {\n379\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Pruning × Recovery Interaction\",\n380\t        \"columns\": [\n381\t          \"Pruning\",\n382\t          \"SFT-Only\",\n383\t          \"GRPO\",\n384\t          \"Δ (GRPO - SFT)\"\n385\t        ],\n386\t        \"rows\": [\n387\t          [\n388\t            \"RASP_20\",\n389\t            \"57.0%\",\n390\t            \"64.0%\",\n391\t            \"+7.0pp\"\n392\t          ],\n393\t          [\n394\t            \"Standard_20\",\n395\t            \"64.0%\",\n396\t            \"59.0%\",\n397\t            \"-5.0pp\"\n398\t          ],\n399\t          [\n400\t            \"Δ (RASP - Standard)\",\n401\t            \"-7.0pp\",\n402\t            \"+5.0pp\",\n403\t            \"Interaction: 12pp\"\n404\t          ]\n405\t        ]\n406\t      },\n407\t      {\n408\t        \"name\": \"2×2 ANOVA Results\",\n409\t        \"columns\": [\n410\t          \"Source\",\n411\t          \"F\",\n412\t          \"p\",\n413\t          \"η²\"\n414\t        ],\n415\t        \"rows\": [\n416\t          [\n417\t            \"Pruning Method\",\n418\t            1.2,\n419\t            0.28,\n420\t            0.02\n421\t          ],\n422\t          [\n423\t            \"Recovery Method\",\n424\t            0.8,\n425\t            0.38,\n426\t            0.01\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"Pruning × Recovery\",\n430\t            8.4,\n431\t            0.008,\n432\t            0.12\n433\t          ]\n434\t        ]\n435\t      }\n436\t    ],\n437\t    \"figures\": [],\n438\t    \"analysis\": \"这是整篇paper在median档下最clean的result。交叉效应12pp且p<0.01。 ANOVA显示main effects均不显著——pruning method和recovery method 各自不决定accuracy，但interaction dominates。 这直接支持Claim 3：\\\"recovery method conditions optimal pruning order\\\"。 Narrative pivot到interaction作为核心贡献完全justified。 需要注意：这个ANOVA是在N=1319的single eval上做的， 严格来说需要multi-seed validation。但effect size足够大(12pp) 使reviewer likely接受。\\n\\n\\n这是median档最强claim的支撑实验。已有N=100数据：sft_rasp_20=57%， sft_standard_20=64%。N=1319预期保持这个pattern。 SFT下Standard优于RASP 7pp——方向与GRPO完全相反（GRPO下RASP优5pp）。 交叉效应显著(p=0.008)：pruning method × recovery method interaction 在2×2 ANOVA中eta²=0.12（medium effect size）。 机制解释：SFT通过teacher-forcing扩展correct paths——Standard保留的 high-importance结构更适合supervised signal的gradient flow。 GRPO通过reward signal压缩incorrect paths——RASP保留的functionally unique 结构更好地维持了RLVR exploration的diversity。 这个crossover是genuinely novel的发现，且mechanistically interpretable。\\n\"\n439\t  },\n440\t  {\n441\t    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Pipeline\",\n442\t    \"description\": \"25% sparsity下的完整pipeline：RASP和Standard prune → eval → SFT → GRPO。 测试sparsity level robustness。\\n\",\n443\t    \"results\": {\n444\t      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.18,\n445\t      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.14,\n446\t      \"rasp_25_postprune_gap_pp\": 4,\n447\t      \"rasp_25_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.48,\n448\t      \"standard_25_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.55,\n449\t      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.55,\n450\t      \"standard_25_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.48,\n451\t      \"grpo_recovery_gap_25_pp\": 7,\n452\t      \"interaction_maintained\": true\n453\t    },\n454\t    \"tables\": [\n455\t      {\n456\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\",\n457\t        \"columns\": [\n458\t          \"Model\",\n459\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n460\t          \"Post-SFT\",\n461\t          \"Post-GRPO\"\n462\t        ],\n463\t        \"rows\": [\n464\t          [\n465\t            \"RASP_25\",\n466\t            \"18.0%\",\n467\t            \"48.0%\",\n468\t            \"55.0%\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          [\n471\t            \"Standard_25\",\n472\t            \"14.0%\",\n473\t            \"55.0%\",\n474\t            \"48.0%\"\n475\t          ]\n476\t        ]\n477\t      }\n478\t    ],\n479\t    \"figures\": [],\n480\t    \"analysis\": \"25%数据强化两个narrative：(1) RASP advantage scales with sparsity， (2) interaction effect is robust across sparsity levels。 但overall recovery降低——55% vs 79% dense = 70% retention， 接近practical utility threshold。这为30% probe设定预期。\\n\\n\\n25% sparsity移除更多结构，post-prune accuracy进一步下降。 RASP 18% vs Standard 14%——gap从3pp扩大到4pp因为更多pruning decisions 意味着CKA signal有更多机会区分functionally redundant vs unique。 Recovery趋势与20%一致但更pronounced：SFT下Standard优7pp (55% vs 48%)， GRPO下RASP优7pp (55% vs 48%)。交互效应维持甚至增强。 GRPO recovery gap从5pp扩大到7pp——在higher sparsity下， 保留functionally unique结构的优势更明显因为GRPO需要更多structural diversity 来maintain exploration。但overall recovery ceiling降低（55% vs 64% at 20%）， 符合\\\"more pruning = harder recovery\\\"的general expectation。\\n\"\n481\t  },\n482\t  {\n483\t    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe (Prune + Eval Only)\",\n484\t    \"description\": \"30% sparsity下仅prune + eval（不做recovery）。 Map sparsity threshold where both methods approach collapse。\\n\",\n485\t    \"results\": {\n486\t      \"rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.08,\n487\t      \"standard_30_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.03,\n488\t      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n489\t      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.04,\n490\t      \"gap_pp\": 5,\n491\t      \"both_near_collapse\": true\n492\t    },\n493\t    \"tables\": [\n494\t      {\n495\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Sparsity Scaling\",\n496\t        \"columns\": [\n497\t          \"Sparsity\",\n498\t          \"RASP Post-Prune\",\n499\t          \"Standard Post-Prune\",\n500\t          \"Gap (pp)\"\n501\t        ],\n502\t        \"rows\": [\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"20%\",\n505\t            \"30.0%\",\n506\t            \"27.0%\",\n507\t            \"3\"\n508\t          ],\n509\t          [\n510\t            \"25%\",\n511\t            \"18.0%\",\n512\t            \"14.0%\",\n513\t            \"4\"\n514\t          ],\n515\t          [\n516\t            \"30%\",\n517\t            \"8.0%\",\n518\t            \"3.0%\",\n519\t            \"5\"\n520\t          ]\n521\t        ]\n522\t      }\n523\t    ],\n524\t    \"figures\": [],\n525\t    \"analysis\": \"30%数据展示diminishing returns：虽然RASP gap在pp上扩大， 但两者都approaching collapse。This bounds RASP's practical applicability to 20-25% sparsity range for this model。 对论文有价值：shows the method's operating range honestly， 不oversell到high sparsity。\\n\\n\\n已有D005实验在35% sparsity显示collapse。30%接近threshold： RASP勉强维持8%（generation部分functional但reasoning严重受损）， Standard接近完全collapse (3%)。Gap扩大到5pp但两者都在near-random水平。 EOS rate差异说明RASP保留了basic generation ability而Standard已崩溃。 这个数据点重要性在于showing the trend：20% (30/27) → 25% (18/14) → 30% (8/3)， RASP advantage在pp上持续但两者都approaching zero。 Recovery at 30%可能仍然possible for RASP but infeasible for Standard—— 但不做recovery所以这是speculative。\\n\"\n526\t  },\n527\t  {\n528\t    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU)\",\n529\t    \"description\": \"Best recovered config (RASP_20 post-GRPO) 在OOD benchmarks上评估。 Shows recovery generalizes beyond GSM8K。\\n\",\n530\t    \"results\": {\n531\t      \"rasp_grpo_math500\": 0.38,\n532\t      \"standard_grpo_math500\": 0.33,\n533\t      \"rasp_grpo_humaneval\": 0.42,\n534\t      \"standard_grpo_humaneval\": 0.41,\n535\t      \"rasp_grpo_mmlu\": 0.55,\n536\t      \"standard_grpo_mmlu\": 0.54,\n537\t      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n538\t      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n539\t      \"dense_mmlu\": 0.62,\n540\t      \"math500_rasp_advantage_pp\": 5,\n541\t      \"humaneval_rasp_advantage_pp\": 1,\n542\t      \"mmlu_rasp_advantage_pp\": 1\n543\t    },\n544\t    \"tables\": [\n545\t      {\n546\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: OOD Evaluation\",\n547\t        \"columns\": [\n548\t          \"Benchmark\",\n549\t          \"Dense\",\n550\t          \"RASP+GRPO\",\n551\t          \"Standard+GRPO\",\n552\t          \"Δ (pp)\"\n553\t        ],\n554\t        \"rows\": [\n555\t          [\n556\t            \"GSM8K\",\n557\t            \"79.0%\",\n558\t            \"64.0%\",\n559\t            \"59.0%\",\n560\t            \"+5\"\n561\t          ],\n562\t          [\n563\t            \"MATH-500\",\n564\t            \"52.0%\",\n565\t            \"38.0%\",\n566\t            \"33.0%\",\n567\t            \"+5\"\n568\t          ],\n569\t          [\n570\t            \"HumanEval\",\n571\t            \"58.0%\",\n572\t            \"42.0%\",\n573\t            \"41.0%\",\n574\t            \"+1\"\n575\t          ],\n576\t          [\n577\t            \"MMLU\",\n578\t            \"62.0%\",\n579\t            \"55.0%\",\n580\t            \"54.0%\",\n581\t            \"+1\"\n582\t          ]\n583\t        ]\n584\t      }\n585\t    ],\n586\t    \"figures\": [],\n587\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD结果是mixed——这是median档的定义特征。MATH-500优势支持\\\"reasoning-specific\\\" narrative但HumanEval/MMLU无差异限制了generalization claim。 论文framing需要careful：CKA-aware pruning preserves math reasoning structures specifically，而非general capabilities。这actually strengthens mechanistic story （CKA signal captures reasoning-specific redundancy），但limits practical impact。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义MATH-500上RASP advantage 0-8pp，HumanEval无差异。 MATH-500上RASP优5pp (38% vs 33%)——MATH-500与GSM8K同domain (math reasoning)， CKA-aware pruning保留的reasoning structures对math reasoning broadly有效。 HumanEval (code)上近乎无差异(1pp)——coding ability依赖不同的structural components， CKA signal对code generation无特异性。MMLU (knowledge)同样无差异—— pruning主要影响reasoning而非factual knowledge retrieval。 Dense model的retention：MATH-500 73% (38/52)，HumanEval 72% (42/58)， MMLU 89% (55/62)。MMLU retention最高因为knowledge更robust to pruning。\\n\"\n588\t  },\n589\t  {\n590\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n591\t    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning baseline。 Lower priority than GRASPrune。\\n\",\n592\t    \"results\": {\n593\t      \"bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.2,\n594\t      \"bonsai_20_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.52,\n595\t      \"bonsai_20_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.5\n596\t    },\n597\t    \"tables\": [],\n598\t    \"figures\": [],\n599\t    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai是completeness baseline。不改变ranking或narrative。 如果space tight可以放appendix。\\n\\n\\nBonsai是gradient-free方法，与magnitude-only类似但有structural constraints。 Post-prune 20%——低于RASP (30%)和Standard (27%)但高于GRASPrune (8%)。 Gradient-free意味着它not as targeted但also avoids gradient noise。 Recovery到50%——低于RASP (64%)和Standard (59%)。 在median档下Bonsai提供another data point但不改变main narrative。 其主要价值是showing that even simple methods achieve reasonable recovery， reinforcing \\\"GRPO is broadly effective\\\" message。\\n\"\n600\t  },\n601\t  {\n602\t    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n603\t    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity。 验证CKA-based scoring的稳定性。\\n\",\n604\t    \"results\": {\n605\t      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.91,\n606\t      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.93,\n607\t      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.97,\n608\t      \"cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_1024\": -0.01,\n609\t      \"cka_compute_time_256\": \"8min\",\n610\t      \"cka_compute_time_512\": \"15min\",\n611\t      \"cka_compute_time_1024\": \"28min\"\n612\t    },\n613\t    \"tables\": [\n614\t      {\n615\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: CKA Stability\",\n616\t        \"columns\": [\n617\t          \"Calibration Size\",\n618\t          \"Rank Corr vs 1024\",\n619\t          \"Post-Prune Acc\",\n620\t          \"Compute Time\"\n621\t        ],\n622\t        \"rows\": [\n623\t          [\n624\t            256,\n625\t            0.93,\n626\t            \"29.0%\",\n627\t            \"8 min\"\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            512,\n631\t            0.97,\n632\t            \"30.0%\",\n633\t            \"15 min\"\n634\t          ],\n635\t          [\n636\t            1024,\n637\t            \"1.00 (ref)\",\n638\t            \"30.0%\",\n639\t            \"28 min\"\n640\t          ]\n641\t        ]\n642\t      }\n643\t    ],\n644\t    \"figures\": [],\n645\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring是stable enough for practical use。256 samples提供 reasonable trade-off（8min compute, 93% rank preservation）。 这addresses reviewer concern about CKA overhead。\\n\\n\\nCKA基于kernel method，inherently对sample size robust。 Split-half ρ=0.91 > 0.9 threshold说明scoring是reproducible。 256 vs 1024 samples导致accuracy仅差1pp——说明256 samples足够 获得near-optimal pruning decision。这支持practical applicability （CKA computation cost可控）。Cal 512→1024的marginal gain minimal (ρ=0.97)， 说明diminishing returns。Compute time与sample size近线性。 Median档下这些数字都\\\"okay but not impressive\\\"——ρ=0.91不是0.98， 有些noise在CKA estimation中。\\n\"\n646\t  },\n647\t  {\n648\t    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n649\t    \"description\": \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} in S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α at 20% sparsity。 Post-prune GSM8K eval for each。\\n\",\n650\t    \"results\": {\n651\t      \"alpha_0_gsm8k\": 0.27,\n652\t      \"alpha_0p25_gsm8k\": 0.28,\n653\t      \"alpha_0p5_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n654\t      \"alpha_1p0_gsm8k\": 0.3,\n655\t      \"alpha_2p0_gsm8k\": 0.34,\n656\t      \"alpha_4p0_gsm8k\": 0.4,\n657\t      \"optimal_alpha\": 4.0,\n658\t      \"optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp\": 13,\n659\t      \"curve_shape\": \"monotonically increasing but noisy\",\n660\t      \"alpha_1_vs_optimal_gap_pp\": 10,\n661\t      \"seed_sensitivity_at_optimal\": \"±3pp across 3 seeds\"\n662\t    },\n663\t    \"tables\": [\n664\t      {\n665\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: α Ablation\",\n666\t        \"columns\": [\n667\t          \"α\",\n668\t          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n669\t          \"vs α=0 Δ\"\n670\t        ],\n671\t        \"rows\": [\n672\t          [\n673\t            \"0 (importance-only)\",\n674\t            \"27.0%\",\n675\t            \"—\"\n676\t          ],\n677\t          [\n678\t            0.25,\n679\t            \"28.0%\",\n680\t            \"+1pp\"\n681\t          ],\n682\t          [\n683\t            0.5,\n684\t            \"29.0%\",\n685\t            \"+2pp\"\n686\t          ],\n687\t          [\n688\t            1.0,\n689\t            \"30.0%\",\n690\t            \"+3pp\"\n691\t          ],\n692\t          [\n693\t            2.0,\n694\t            \"34.0%\",\n695\t            \"+7pp\"\n696\t          ],\n697\t          [\n698\t            4.0,\n699\t            \"40.0%\",\n700\t            \"+13pp\"\n701\t          ]\n702\t        ]\n703\t      }\n704\t    ],\n705\t    \"figures\": [],\n706\t    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是second practical contribution。Key findings： (1) CKA signal consistently helps (monotonic improvement with α)， (2) default α=1 is suboptimal, α≈2-4 better， (3) but optimal α is seed-sensitive。 这suggests adaptive α selection as future work。 对Claim 1的影响：RASP with α=4 achieves 40% post-prune (vs Standard 27%)—— gap扩大到13pp，比α=1的3pp gap大得多。如果用optimal α，Claim 1显著增强。 但需要honest discussion of seed sensitivity和overfitting risk （α是在post-prune accuracy上tuned的，可能不generalize to recovery）。\\n\\n\\n已有初步数据：alpha_ablation_westd_cal256显示α=4.0给出40% accuracy (highest)。 α=0等价于importance-only (Standard)，预期27%——与Standard结果一致。 α从0到4单调递增说明CKA signal consistently有益。但median档的nuance： 曲线噪声较多——α=0.25和α=0.5之间差异仅1pp，可能在noise range内。 Optimal α=4.0远高于default α=1——说明CKA signal应该被more heavily weighted， current RASP default (α=1)是suboptimal。13pp gap (α=0 vs α=4)比 median档定义的5-10pp范围更大——但这与已有实验数据一致(40% vs 27%)。 Seed sensitivity ±3pp at α=4说明optimal point不完全stable—— 某些seed下α=2可能更好。这limits the precision of α recommendation。\\n\"\n707\t  },\n708\t  {\n709\t    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n710\t    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput对比：dense、RASP_20、Standard_20。 Structured pruning的practical motivation需要efficiency evidence。\\n\",\n711\t    \"results\": {\n712\t      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 28.5,\n713\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 23.8,\n714\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 23.5,\n715\t      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 35.1,\n716\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 42.0,\n717\t      \"standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 42.6,\n718\t      \"rasp_speedup_ratio\": 1.2,\n719\t      \"standard_speedup_ratio\": 1.21,\n720\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff\": \"negligible\",\n721\t      \"batch_size_tested\": [\n722\t        1,\n723\t        4,\n724\t        8\n725\t      ],\n726\t      \"speedup_at_batch_8\": 1.18\n727\t    },\n728\t    \"tables\": [\n729\t      {\n730\t        \"name\": \"Table 12: Inference Efficiency\",\n731\t        \"columns\": [\n732\t          \"Model\",\n733\t          \"Latency (ms/token)\",\n734\t          \"Speedup\",\n735\t          \"Throughput (tok/s)\"\n736\t        ],\n737\t        \"rows\": [\n738\t          [\n739\t            \"Dense\",\n740\t            28.5,\n741\t            \"1.00×\",\n742\t            35.1\n743\t          ],\n744\t          [\n745\t            \"RASP_20\",\n746\t            23.8,\n747\t            \"1.20×\",\n748\t            42.0\n749\t          ],\n750\t          [\n751\t            \"Standard_20\",\n752\t            23.5,\n753\t            \"1.21×\",\n754\t            42.6\n755\t          ]\n756\t        ]\n757\t      }\n758\t    ],\n759\t    \"figures\": [],\n760\t    \"analysis\": \"1.20x speedup是modest但real。对于reasoning model的long generation (often 500-2000 tokens)，累积time saving significant。 RASP和Standard speedup差异negligible——这是好消息（RASP没有efficiency cost） 也是expected（same sparsity level）。 论文中作为practical motivation section的supporting data。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义speedup ratio在[1.15, 1.25]。取1.20x for RASP。 20% structured sparsity移除20% MLP channel groups——理论speedup上限 接近1.25x (MLP占total compute ~67%，移除20% MLP ≈ 13% total reduction)。 实际1.20x低于理论上限因为：(1) attention compute不变， (2) memory bandwidth bottleneck at small batch sizes， (3) kernel launch overhead不随width减少。 RASP和Standard speedup几乎相同(1.20 vs 1.21)——两者移除相同数量的结构， 只是选择了不同的结构。Pruning method不影响inference speed。 Batch size 8时speedup略降(1.18x)——更compute-bound时 width reduction的relative benefit减少。\\n\"\n761\t  },\n762\t  {\n763\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n764\t    \"description\": \"20% unstructured (magnitude-based) pruning baseline。 Calibrate structured vs unstructured gap。\\n\",\n765\t    \"results\": {\n766\t      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.68,\n767\t      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.7,\n768\t      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.62,\n769\t      \"unstructured_20_speedup_ratio\": 1.0,\n770\t      \"unstructured_vs_dense_retention_postprune\": 0.86,\n771\t      \"unstructured_vs_rasp_structured_postprune_gap\": 38\n772\t    },\n773\t    \"tables\": [\n774\t      {\n775\t        \"name\": \"Table 13: Structured vs Unstructured\",\n776\t        \"columns\": [\n777\t          \"Method\",\n778\t          \"Type\",\n779\t          \"Post-Prune\",\n780\t          \"Post-GRPO\",\n781\t          \"Speedup\"\n782\t        ],\n783\t        \"rows\": [\n784\t          [\n785\t            \"RASP_20\",\n786\t            \"Structured\",\n787\t            \"30.0%\",\n788\t            \"64.0%\",\n789\t            \"1.20×\"\n790\t          ],\n791\t          [\n792\t            \"Standard_20\",\n793\t            \"Structured\",\n794\t            \"27.0%\",\n795\t            \"59.0%\",\n796\t            \"1.21×\"\n797\t          ],\n798\t          [\n799\t            \"Magnitude_20\",\n800\t            \"Unstructured\",\n801\t            \"68.0%\",\n802\t            \"62.0%\",\n803\t            \"1.00×\"\n804\t          ]\n805\t        ]\n806\t      }\n807\t    ],\n808\t    \"figures\": [],\n809\t    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured baseline frames the paper's contribution： structured pruning trades post-prune accuracy for real speedup， 但needs intelligent structure selection (RASP) and RLVR recovery (GRPO) to close the accuracy gap。RASP+GRPO (64%) approaches unstructured (62%) while delivering 1.20x speedup——this is the practical value proposition。 Interesting：RASP+GRPO actually slightly beats unstructured+GRPO (64% vs 62%)。 这可能是noise但也可能说明structured pruning creates better GRPO training dynamics。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured 20% pruning保留much more accuracy post-prune (68% vs 30% RASP) 因为individual weight zeroing far less disruptive than removing entire channel groups。 Post-SFT仅微增到70%（already high baseline）。 Post-GRPO actually slightly lower (62%)——可能因为sparse weights的gradient flow 不如dense结构适合RLVR的exploration-exploitation dynamics。 关键：unstructured pruning无法获得real speedup (1.0x)因为sparse operations 在standard GPU hardware上不加速。这justifies structured pruning research。 Median档预期post_grpo 0.58-0.66，取0.62。 GRPO对unstructured model的recovery有限因为post-prune accuracy已经high (68%)， \\\"ceiling effect\\\"限制了further improvement，且部分accuracy可能lost to GRPO's exploration noise on already-functional model。\\n\"\n810\t  },\n811\t  {\n812\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n813\t    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered Standard model (64% GSM8K) 在MATH-500和HumanEval上评估。 Check if 1%→64% SFT jump is genuine reasoning recovery vs GSM8K memorization。\\n\",\n814\t    \"results\": {\n815\t      \"sft_standard_math500\": 0.3,\n816\t      \"sft_standard_humaneval\": 0.35,\n817\t      \"sft_standard_gsm8k_ref\": 0.64,\n818\t      \"sft_rasp_math500\": 0.28,\n819\t      \"sft_rasp_humaneval\": 0.33,\n820\t      \"sft_rasp_gsm8k_ref\": 0.57,\n821\t      \"dense_math500_ref\": 0.52,\n822\t      \"dense_humaneval_ref\": 0.58,\n823\t      \"math500_retention_standard_sft\": 0.58,\n824\t      \"humaneval_retention_standard_sft\": 0.6\n825\t    },\n826\t    \"tables\": [\n827\t      {\n828\t        \"name\": \"Table 14: SFT Recovery OOD Check\",\n829\t        \"columns\": [\n830\t          \"Model\",\n831\t          \"GSM8K\",\n832\t          \"MATH-500\",\n833\t          \"HumanEval\"\n834\t        ],\n835\t        \"rows\": [\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"Dense\",\n838\t            \"79.0%\",\n839\t            \"52.0%\",\n840\t            \"58.0%\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"SFT-Standard\",\n844\t            \"64.0%\",\n845\t            \"30.0%\",\n846\t            \"35.0%\"\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            \"SFT-RASP\",\n850\t            \"57.0%\",\n851\t            \"28.0%\",\n852\t            \"33.0%\"\n853\t          ],\n854\t          [\n855\t            \"GRPO-RASP\",\n856\t            \"64.0%\",\n857\t            \"38.0%\",\n858\t            \"42.0%\"\n859\t          ],\n860\t          [\n861\t            \"GRPO-Standard\",\n862\t            \"59.0%\",\n863\t            \"33.0%\",\n864\t            \"41.0%\"\n865\t          ]\n866\t        ]\n867\t      }\n868\t    ],\n869\t    \"figures\": [],\n870\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT recovery不是memorization——OOD performance confirms genuine recovery。 但GRPO recovery consistently delivers higher OOD retention， especially on MATH-500 (38% vs 30% for best SFT)。 This adds to Claim 3：GRPO不仅在GSM8K上favor RASP， 在OOD上也delivers deeper、more generalizable recovery。\\n\\nStandard SFT 64% GSM8K的1%→64%跳跃确实suspicious——但SFT是supervised training， 能够快速恢复format和basic arithmetic。MATH-500上30% (vs dense 52%) 说明SFT recovery是genuine但partial——不仅是GSM8K pattern memorization， 因为MATH-500难度更高，30%仍代表real reasoning能力（random baseline ~5%）。 HumanEval 35%同样说明generalized recovery。 关键comparison：SFT-Standard MATH-500 (30%) vs GRPO-RASP MATH-500 (38%)—— GRPO recovery在OOD上更robust，支持\\\"RLVR enables deeper recovery\\\"的argument。 但SFT-Standard > SFT-RASP on MATH-500 (30% vs 28%)—— SFT recovery maintain Standard's advantage even OOD。Interaction story holds。\\n\"\n871\t  }\n872\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80acf845-bd40-40fe-a62c-7979cde6caad","uuid":"23aa5be1-f34f-41e7-aa2c-89ca3952802a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:41:50.058Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\",\n    \"description\": \"对baseline dense模型、RASP_20、Standard_20在完整GSM8K test set (1319 samples)上评估。 替代现有N=100的初步数据，获得±2.4pp的tight CI。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_dense_gsm8k_1319\": 0.79,\n      \"rasp_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.3,\n      \"standard_20_gsm8k_1319\": 0.27,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 3,\n      \"rasp_ci_95\": [\n        0.276,\n        0.324\n      ],\n      \"standard_ci_95\": [\n        0.246,\n        0.294\n      ],\n      \"gap_p_value_single_seed\": 0.11\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Accuracy\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"vs Dense Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense Baseline\",\n            \"79.0%\",\n            \"[76.8, 81.2]\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"[27.6, 32.4]\",\n            \"-49.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"[24.6, 29.4]\",\n            \"-52.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3pp gap在N=1319下仍不够statistically significant (单seed)。 这确认了median档预期：需要multi-seed (plan_006)来建立significance。 Post-prune gap本身不是headline claim——recovery后的gap才是。\\n\\n\\nN=100的reeval_postprune_definitive已显示gap为4pp (31% vs 27% on westb)。 扩展到N=1319后，点估计会regress toward mean——N=100的方差大(±9pp CI)， full eval预期RASP 30%、Standard 27%左右。单seed下CI重叠，p≈0.11不显著， 这正是median档的核心特征：gap真实存在但需要multi-seed才能确认显著性。 Dense baseline 79%与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B已知性能一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Recovery)\",\n    \"description\": \"对所有recovered模型(SFT→GRPO)在完整GSM8K test set上评估。 Paper Table 1的最终数字。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"post_grpo_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n      \"post_grpo_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.59,\n      \"post_sft_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.56,\n      \"post_sft_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n      \"grpo_recovery_gap_pp\": 5,\n      \"grpo_rasp_recovery_from_postprune_pp\": 34,\n      \"grpo_standard_recovery_from_postprune_pp\": 32,\n      \"grpo_rasp_vs_dense_retention\": 0.81,\n      \"grpo_standard_vs_dense_retention\": 0.75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Full Pipeline Results (N=1319)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\",\n          \"Recovery Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"79.0%\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"+34.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"+32.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"关键发现：SFT阶段Standard领先8pp (64% vs 56%)，GRPO阶段RASP反超5pp (64% vs 59%)。 这个crossover是Claim 3的核心证据。GRPO gap 5pp虽然modest，但方向一致且N=1319下 statistically significant。Narrative pivot到\\\"pruning-recovery interaction\\\"合理。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义GRPO recovery gap为2-8pp。取中值5pp：RASP 64%、Standard 59%。 两者都从post-prune状态大幅恢复（+34pp和+32pp），说明GRPO对两种pruned结构 都有效——但RASP保留的functionally unique结构给GRPO多提供了5pp的恢复空间。 SFT-only数据(plan_009)会反转这个关系，构成交互效应的核心证据。 Recovery gap有限但在N=1319下CI不重叠（64%±2.6 vs 59%±2.7）， 可达p<0.05显著性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline： prune → eval → SFT → GRPO recovery。Primary external baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319\": 0.08,\n      \"grasp_20_postprune_eos_rate\": 0.05,\n      \"grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319\": 0.42,\n      \"grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319\": 0.52,\n      \"grasp_sft_recovery_pp\": 34,\n      \"grasp_grpo_recovery_from_sft_pp\": 10,\n      \"grasp_vs_rasp_grpo_gap_pp\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"56.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRASPrune_20\",\n            \"8.0%\",\n            \"42.0%\",\n            \"52.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune作为baseline提供两个关键insight：(1) post-prune accuracy不能直接预测 recovery ceiling（GRASPrune 8%→52%，恢复44pp；RASP 30%→64%，恢复34pp）， 说明recovery mechanism非线性。(2) 即使是SOTA importance-based pruning， 不考虑CKA信号也会移除GRPO-critical结构。 但median档下这个narrative需要nuance：Standard (27%→59%) recovery也不错， 说明CKA signal的贡献是incremental而非decisive。\\n\\n\\n已有初步数据：grasp_baseline_westd显示50-sample post-prune accuracy仅8%， EOS rate 2%，avg_len 4019——与Standard_20的initial状态类似（generation崩溃）。 Median档预期GRASPrune post-prune远差于RASP (8% vs 31%)因为GRASPrune 优化budgeted importance但不考虑functional redundancy，会移除functionally unique的结构。SFT恢复到42%（从8%有大幅提升，说明结构本身没有完全损坏， 只是generation能力崩溃）。GRPO进一步恢复到52%，但仍低于RASP的64%。 关键：GRASPrune+GRPO (52%) vs Standard+GRPO (59%)的gap说明 pruning method确实影响recovery ceiling，且GRASPrune的\\\"better importance scoring\\\" 不能弥补missing CKA signal。但GRASPrune+GRPO也在恢复（不是完全fail）， 这符合median档\\\"GRPO broadly effective\\\"的假设。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"RASP_20 + Standard_20在5个random seeds下的post-prune GSM8K eval。 建立robust方差估计和pairwise significance。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_seed_results\": [\n        0.3,\n        0.28,\n        0.31,\n        0.29,\n        0.32\n      ],\n      \"standard_20_seed_results\": [\n        0.27,\n        0.29,\n        0.26,\n        0.28,\n        0.25\n      ],\n      \"rasp_20_mean\": 0.3,\n      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.015,\n      \"standard_20_mean\": 0.27,\n      \"standard_20_std\": 0.016,\n      \"gap_mean_pp\": 3.0,\n      \"gap_p_value_paired_t\": 0.03,\n      \"gap_p_value_wilcoxon\": 0.06,\n      \"seeds_with_gap_lt_2pp\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"RASP_20\",\n          \"Standard_20\",\n          \"Gap (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"+3.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            123,\n            \"28.0%\",\n            \"29.0%\",\n            \"-1.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            256,\n            \"31.0%\",\n            \"26.0%\",\n            \"+5.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            789,\n            \"29.0%\",\n            \"28.0%\",\n            \"+1.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1024,\n            \"32.0%\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"+7.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std\",\n            \"30.0±1.5%\",\n            \"27.0±1.6%\",\n            \"+3.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"p (paired t)\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\",\n            \"0.03\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap在统计边界：paired t p=0.03但一个seed显示反转。 这意味着Claim 1必须弱化——不能说\\\"significantly preserves more reasoning ability\\\"， 而应说\\\"tends to preserve more\\\"或\\\"preserves more on average across seeds\\\"。 但重要的是，recovery后的gap可能比post-prune gap更稳定， 因为GRPO amplifies structural advantages。Multi-seed GRPO recovery 数据（如果有budget做）会更有说服力。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义postprune_gap_p_value_5seed为[0.01, 0.08]。取p=0.03 (paired t)。 5-seed方差较大：某些seed下gap缩小到<2pp（seed 2: 28% vs 29%，gap为-1pp， Standard actually高于RASP）。这正是median档\\\"某些seed gap<2pp\\\"的核心特征。 整体mean gap 3pp，paired t-test p=0.03达到conventional significance， 但Wilcoxon(更conservative) p=0.06 marginal。Reviewer可以argue either way。 Std ~1.5%与GSM8K eval的intrinsic noise一致（N=1319下binomial std ≈ 1.3%）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring Ablation (20% Sparsity)\",\n    \"description\": \"在20% sparsity下测试不同scoring方法：magnitude-only、gradient-only、 random pruning。与RASP和Standard对比，隔离CKA的贡献。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.22,\n      \"gradient_only_gsm8k_1319\": 0.28,\n      \"random_pruning_gsm8k_1319\": 0.05,\n      \"rasp_gsm8k_1319_ref\": 0.3,\n      \"standard_gsm8k_1319_ref\": 0.27,\n      \"cka_marginal_contribution_vs_gradient\": 2,\n      \"cka_marginal_contribution_vs_magnitude\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Scoring Method Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scoring\",\n          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n          \"vs RASP Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP (α=1)\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard (gradient+magnitude)\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"-3.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient-only\",\n            \"28.0%\",\n            \"-2.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Magnitude-only\",\n            \"22.0%\",\n            \"-8.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random\",\n            \"5.0%\",\n            \"-25.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA的post-prune marginal contribution仅2pp (vs gradient-only)， Reviewer会质疑是否值得额外的CKA计算开销。Defense需要两个角度： (1) recovery后gap放大（plan_004数据），(2) interaction效应（plan_009）。 Random collapse (5%)提供useful lower bound。 Magnitude-only的劣势支持\\\"importance metric choice matters\\\"的general argument。\\n\\n\\nRandom pruning接近collapse (5%)——随机移除20%结构大概率命中critical components。 Magnitude-only (22%)低于gradient-based (28%)因为weight magnitude在Qwen架构 中不是结构重要性的good proxy（RMSNorm使magnitude scale less informative）。 Gradient-only (28%)接近Standard (27%)是预期的——Standard本身就是gradient-based importance + magnitude的组合。RASP (30%)比gradient-only高2pp， 这就是CKA的marginal contribution。Median档下这个2pp差异modest但方向正确。 关键insight：CKA的价值不在post-prune accuracy的marginal gain， 而在recovery-method-specific的交互效应（plan_009会显示）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h)与recovery后per-structure activation变化的相关性分析。Mixed-effects regression。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_mlp_groups_analyzed\": 784,\n      \"n_pruned_mlp_groups\": 200,\n      \"cka_beta_coefficient\": 0.18,\n      \"cka_beta_p_value\": 0.02,\n      \"cka_incremental_r2\": 0.08,\n      \"full_model_r2\": 0.34,\n      \"weight_norm_beta_p\": 0.001,\n      \"gradient_importance_beta_p\": 0.008,\n      \"activation_magnitude_beta_p\": 0.04,\n      \"cka_weight_norm_correlation\": 0.42,\n      \"vif_cka\": 2.1,\n      \"layer_random_effect_variance\": 0.06\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Mixed-Effects Regression (MLP Groups, N=784)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Predictor\",\n          \"β\",\n          \"SE\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Incremental R²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Weight Norm\",\n            0.31,\n            0.06,\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"14%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gradient Importance\",\n            0.22,\n            0.07,\n            \"0.008\",\n            \"11%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Activation Magnitude\",\n            0.12,\n            0.06,\n            \"0.04\",\n            \"5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA F(h)\",\n            0.18,\n            0.07,\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Layer (random)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"σ²=0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full Model\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"R²=0.34\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA provides statistically significant but modest additional signal。 Weight norm和gradient importance是stronger individual predictors。 共线性(r=0.42)意味着CKA部分captures与weight norm相同的information。 论文中需要honest presentation：CKA is not the strongest predictor， 但它captures unique variance不被其他metrics覆盖。 这支持\\\"CKA as complementary signal\\\"的framing而非\\\"CKA as superior metric\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义CKA beta p在[0.005, 0.05]，incremental R²在[0.05, 0.12]。 取p=0.02, incremental R²=8%。CKA显著但effect size中等。 关键nuance：weight norm (r=0.42 with CKA)也是significant predictor (p=0.001)， incremental R²比CKA高。VIF=2.1说明共线性moderate但未达alarming levels (>5)。 这意味着CKA captures some unique variance (8%)但大部分recoverability 被simpler metrics解释。Layer random effect variance=0.06说明层间差异存在 但不dominant。Full model R²=0.34意味着66%的方差unexplained—— recoverability是complex多因素决定的。 Claim 2必须弱化为\\\"additional predictive signal\\\"而非\\\"stronger predictor\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Same pruned models (RASP_20, Standard_20)，same data budget， SFT-only recovery（no GRPO）。测试recovery method是否改变optimal pruning order。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_only_rasp_gsm8k_1319\": 0.57,\n      \"sft_only_standard_gsm8k_1319\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_standard_advantage_pp\": 7,\n      \"sft_standard_vs_grpo_standard\": \"+5pp\",\n      \"sft_rasp_vs_grpo_rasp\": \"-7pp\",\n      \"interaction_effect_2x2_anova_p\": 0.008,\n      \"interaction_effect_size_eta2\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Pruning × Recovery Interaction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pruning\",\n          \"SFT-Only\",\n          \"GRPO\",\n          \"Δ (GRPO - SFT)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"57.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"+7.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"-5.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Δ (RASP - Standard)\",\n            \"-7.0pp\",\n            \"+5.0pp\",\n            \"Interaction: 12pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"2×2 ANOVA Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Source\",\n          \"F\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"η²\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pruning Method\",\n            1.2,\n            0.28,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recovery Method\",\n            0.8,\n            0.38,\n            0.01\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Pruning × Recovery\",\n            8.4,\n            0.008,\n            0.12\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是整篇paper在median档下最clean的result。交叉效应12pp且p<0.01。 ANOVA显示main effects均不显著——pruning method和recovery method 各自不决定accuracy，但interaction dominates。 这直接支持Claim 3：\\\"recovery method conditions optimal pruning order\\\"。 Narrative pivot到interaction作为核心贡献完全justified。 需要注意：这个ANOVA是在N=1319的single eval上做的， 严格来说需要multi-seed validation。但effect size足够大(12pp) 使reviewer likely接受。\\n\\n\\n这是median档最强claim的支撑实验。已有N=100数据：sft_rasp_20=57%， sft_standard_20=64%。N=1319预期保持这个pattern。 SFT下Standard优于RASP 7pp——方向与GRPO完全相反（GRPO下RASP优5pp）。 交叉效应显著(p=0.008)：pruning method × recovery method interaction 在2×2 ANOVA中eta²=0.12（medium effect size）。 机制解释：SFT通过teacher-forcing扩展correct paths——Standard保留的 high-importance结构更适合supervised signal的gradient flow。 GRPO通过reward signal压缩incorrect paths——RASP保留的functionally unique 结构更好地维持了RLVR exploration的diversity。 这个crossover是genuinely novel的发现，且mechanistically interpretable。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% Sparsity RASP + Standard Pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"25% sparsity下的完整pipeline：RASP和Standard prune → eval → SFT → GRPO。 测试sparsity level robustness。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.18,\n      \"standard_25_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.14,\n      \"rasp_25_postprune_gap_pp\": 4,\n      \"rasp_25_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.48,\n      \"standard_25_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.55,\n      \"rasp_25_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.55,\n      \"standard_25_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.48,\n      \"grpo_recovery_gap_25_pp\": 7,\n      \"interaction_maintained\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: 25% Sparsity Pipeline\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-SFT\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_25\",\n            \"18.0%\",\n            \"48.0%\",\n            \"55.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_25\",\n            \"14.0%\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"48.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25%数据强化两个narrative：(1) RASP advantage scales with sparsity， (2) interaction effect is robust across sparsity levels。 但overall recovery降低——55% vs 79% dense = 70% retention， 接近practical utility threshold。这为30% probe设定预期。\\n\\n\\n25% sparsity移除更多结构，post-prune accuracy进一步下降。 RASP 18% vs Standard 14%——gap从3pp扩大到4pp因为更多pruning decisions 意味着CKA signal有更多机会区分functionally redundant vs unique。 Recovery趋势与20%一致但更pronounced：SFT下Standard优7pp (55% vs 48%)， GRPO下RASP优7pp (55% vs 48%)。交互效应维持甚至增强。 GRPO recovery gap从5pp扩大到7pp——在higher sparsity下， 保留functionally unique结构的优势更明显因为GRPO需要更多structural diversity 来maintain exploration。但overall recovery ceiling降低（55% vs 64% at 20%）， 符合\\\"more pruning = harder recovery\\\"的general expectation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% Sparsity Probe (Prune + Eval Only)\",\n    \"description\": \"30% sparsity下仅prune + eval（不做recovery）。 Map sparsity threshold where both methods approach collapse。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.08,\n      \"standard_30_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.03,\n      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.15,\n      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.04,\n      \"gap_pp\": 5,\n      \"both_near_collapse\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Sparsity Scaling\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sparsity\",\n          \"RASP Post-Prune\",\n          \"Standard Post-Prune\",\n          \"Gap (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"20%\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25%\",\n            \"18.0%\",\n            \"14.0%\",\n            \"4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30%\",\n            \"8.0%\",\n            \"3.0%\",\n            \"5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"30%数据展示diminishing returns：虽然RASP gap在pp上扩大， 但两者都approaching collapse。This bounds RASP's practical applicability to 20-25% sparsity range for this model。 对论文有价值：shows the method's operating range honestly， 不oversell到high sparsity。\\n\\n\\n已有D005实验在35% sparsity显示collapse。30%接近threshold： RASP勉强维持8%（generation部分functional但reasoning严重受损）， Standard接近完全collapse (3%)。Gap扩大到5pp但两者都在near-random水平。 EOS rate差异说明RASP保留了basic generation ability而Standard已崩溃。 这个数据点重要性在于showing the trend：20% (30/27) → 25% (18/14) → 30% (8/3)， RASP advantage在pp上持续但两者都approaching zero。 Recovery at 30%可能仍然possible for RASP but infeasible for Standard—— 但不做recovery所以这是speculative。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval, MMLU)\",\n    \"description\": \"Best recovered config (RASP_20 post-GRPO) 在OOD benchmarks上评估。 Shows recovery generalizes beyond GSM8K。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_grpo_math500\": 0.38,\n      \"standard_grpo_math500\": 0.33,\n      \"rasp_grpo_humaneval\": 0.42,\n      \"standard_grpo_humaneval\": 0.41,\n      \"rasp_grpo_mmlu\": 0.55,\n      \"standard_grpo_mmlu\": 0.54,\n      \"dense_math500\": 0.52,\n      \"dense_humaneval\": 0.58,\n      \"dense_mmlu\": 0.62,\n      \"math500_rasp_advantage_pp\": 5,\n      \"humaneval_rasp_advantage_pp\": 1,\n      \"mmlu_rasp_advantage_pp\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: OOD Evaluation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Dense\",\n          \"RASP+GRPO\",\n          \"Standard+GRPO\",\n          \"Δ (pp)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"79.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"+5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MATH-500\",\n            \"52.0%\",\n            \"38.0%\",\n            \"33.0%\",\n            \"+5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            \"58.0%\",\n            \"42.0%\",\n            \"41.0%\",\n            \"+1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"62.0%\",\n            \"55.0%\",\n            \"54.0%\",\n            \"+1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD结果是mixed——这是median档的定义特征。MATH-500优势支持\\\"reasoning-specific\\\" narrative但HumanEval/MMLU无差异限制了generalization claim。 论文framing需要careful：CKA-aware pruning preserves math reasoning structures specifically，而非general capabilities。这actually strengthens mechanistic story （CKA signal captures reasoning-specific redundancy），但limits practical impact。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义MATH-500上RASP advantage 0-8pp，HumanEval无差异。 MATH-500上RASP优5pp (38% vs 33%)——MATH-500与GSM8K同domain (math reasoning)， CKA-aware pruning保留的reasoning structures对math reasoning broadly有效。 HumanEval (code)上近乎无差异(1pp)——coding ability依赖不同的structural components， CKA signal对code generation无特异性。MMLU (knowledge)同样无差异—— pruning主要影响reasoning而非factual knowledge retrieval。 Dense model的retention：MATH-500 73% (38/52)，HumanEval 72% (42/58)， MMLU 89% (55/62)。MMLU retention最高因为knowledge更robust to pruning。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai Baseline 20% Sparsity\",\n    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025) gradient-free structured pruning baseline。 Lower priority than GRASPrune。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.2,\n      \"bonsai_20_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.52,\n      \"bonsai_20_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai是completeness baseline。不改变ranking或narrative。 如果space tight可以放appendix。\\n\\n\\nBonsai是gradient-free方法，与magnitude-only类似但有structural constraints。 Post-prune 20%——低于RASP (30%)和Standard (27%)但高于GRASPrune (8%)。 Gradient-free意味着它not as targeted但also avoids gradient noise。 Recovery到50%——低于RASP (64%)和Standard (59%)。 在median档下Bonsai提供another data point但不改变main narrative。 其主要价值是showing that even simple methods achieve reasonable recovery， reinforcing \\\"GRPO is broadly effective\\\" message。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA Reliability Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity。 验证CKA-based scoring的稳定性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.91,\n      \"cal_256_vs_512_rank_corr\": 0.93,\n      \"cal_512_vs_1024_rank_corr\": 0.97,\n      \"cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_1024\": -0.01,\n      \"cka_compute_time_256\": \"8min\",\n      \"cka_compute_time_512\": \"15min\",\n      \"cka_compute_time_1024\": \"28min\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: CKA Stability\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Calibration Size\",\n          \"Rank Corr vs 1024\",\n          \"Post-Prune Acc\",\n          \"Compute Time\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            256,\n            0.93,\n            \"29.0%\",\n            \"8 min\"\n          ],\n          [\n            512,\n            0.97,\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"15 min\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1024,\n            \"1.00 (ref)\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"28 min\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring是stable enough for practical use。256 samples提供 reasonable trade-off（8min compute, 93% rank preservation）。 这addresses reviewer concern about CKA overhead。\\n\\n\\nCKA基于kernel method，inherently对sample size robust。 Split-half ρ=0.91 > 0.9 threshold说明scoring是reproducible。 256 vs 1024 samples导致accuracy仅差1pp——说明256 samples足够 获得near-optimal pruning decision。这支持practical applicability （CKA computation cost可控）。Cal 512→1024的marginal gain minimal (ρ=0.97)， 说明diminishing returns。Compute time与sample size近线性。 Median档下这些数字都\\\"okay but not impressive\\\"——ρ=0.91不是0.98， 有些noise在CKA estimation中。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"α Sensitivity Ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} in S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α at 20% sparsity。 Post-prune GSM8K eval for each。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpha_0_gsm8k\": 0.27,\n      \"alpha_0p25_gsm8k\": 0.28,\n      \"alpha_0p5_gsm8k\": 0.29,\n      \"alpha_1p0_gsm8k\": 0.3,\n      \"alpha_2p0_gsm8k\": 0.34,\n      \"alpha_4p0_gsm8k\": 0.4,\n      \"optimal_alpha\": 4.0,\n      \"optimal_vs_alpha0_gap_pp\": 13,\n      \"curve_shape\": \"monotonically increasing but noisy\",\n      \"alpha_1_vs_optimal_gap_pp\": 10,\n      \"seed_sensitivity_at_optimal\": \"±3pp across 3 seeds\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: α Ablation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"α\",\n          \"Post-Prune GSM8K\",\n          \"vs α=0 Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (importance-only)\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.25,\n            \"28.0%\",\n            \"+1pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            \"29.0%\",\n            \"+2pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"+3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2.0,\n            \"34.0%\",\n            \"+7pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4.0,\n            \"40.0%\",\n            \"+13pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"α ablation是second practical contribution。Key findings： (1) CKA signal consistently helps (monotonic improvement with α)， (2) default α=1 is suboptimal, α≈2-4 better， (3) but optimal α is seed-sensitive。 这suggests adaptive α selection as future work。 对Claim 1的影响：RASP with α=4 achieves 40% post-prune (vs Standard 27%)—— gap扩大到13pp，比α=1的3pp gap大得多。如果用optimal α，Claim 1显著增强。 但需要honest discussion of seed sensitivity和overfitting risk （α是在post-prune accuracy上tuned的，可能不generalize to recovery）。\\n\\n\\n已有初步数据：alpha_ablation_westd_cal256显示α=4.0给出40% accuracy (highest)。 α=0等价于importance-only (Standard)，预期27%——与Standard结果一致。 α从0到4单调递增说明CKA signal consistently有益。但median档的nuance： 曲线噪声较多——α=0.25和α=0.5之间差异仅1pp，可能在noise range内。 Optimal α=4.0远高于default α=1——说明CKA signal应该被more heavily weighted， current RASP default (α=1)是suboptimal。13pp gap (α=0 vs α=4)比 median档定义的5-10pp范围更大——但这与已有实验数据一致(40% vs 27%)。 Seed sensitivity ±3pp at α=4说明optimal point不完全stable—— 某些seed下α=2可能更好。这limits the precision of α recommendation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference Speedup Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Wall-clock latency + throughput对比：dense、RASP_20、Standard_20。 Structured pruning的practical motivation需要efficiency evidence。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms_per_token\": 28.5,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 23.8,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms_per_token\": 23.5,\n      \"dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 35.1,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 42.0,\n      \"standard_20_throughput_tokens_per_sec\": 42.6,\n      \"rasp_speedup_ratio\": 1.2,\n      \"standard_speedup_ratio\": 1.21,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff\": \"negligible\",\n      \"batch_size_tested\": [\n        1,\n        4,\n        8\n      ],\n      \"speedup_at_batch_8\": 1.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 12: Inference Efficiency\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Latency (ms/token)\",\n          \"Speedup\",\n          \"Throughput (tok/s)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            28.5,\n            \"1.00×\",\n            35.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            23.8,\n            \"1.20×\",\n            42.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            23.5,\n            \"1.21×\",\n            42.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"1.20x speedup是modest但real。对于reasoning model的long generation (often 500-2000 tokens)，累积time saving significant。 RASP和Standard speedup差异negligible——这是好消息（RASP没有efficiency cost） 也是expected（same sparsity level）。 论文中作为practical motivation section的supporting data。\\n\\n\\nMedian档定义speedup ratio在[1.15, 1.25]。取1.20x for RASP。 20% structured sparsity移除20% MLP channel groups——理论speedup上限 接近1.25x (MLP占total compute ~67%，移除20% MLP ≈ 13% total reduction)。 实际1.20x低于理论上限因为：(1) attention compute不变， (2) memory bandwidth bottleneck at small batch sizes， (3) kernel launch overhead不随width减少。 RASP和Standard speedup几乎相同(1.20 vs 1.21)——两者移除相同数量的结构， 只是选择了不同的结构。Pruning method不影响inference speed。 Batch size 8时speedup略降(1.18x)——更compute-bound时 width reduction的relative benefit减少。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\",\n    \"description\": \"20% unstructured (magnitude-based) pruning baseline。 Calibrate structured vs unstructured gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k\": 0.68,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_sft_gsm8k\": 0.7,\n      \"unstructured_20_post_grpo_gsm8k\": 0.62,\n      \"unstructured_20_speedup_ratio\": 1.0,\n      \"unstructured_vs_dense_retention_postprune\": 0.86,\n      \"unstructured_vs_rasp_structured_postprune_gap\": 38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 13: Structured vs Unstructured\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Type\",\n          \"Post-Prune\",\n          \"Post-GRPO\",\n          \"Speedup\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RASP_20\",\n            \"Structured\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"1.20×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Standard_20\",\n            \"Structured\",\n            \"27.0%\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"1.21×\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Magnitude_20\",\n            \"Unstructured\",\n            \"68.0%\",\n            \"62.0%\",\n            \"1.00×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Unstructured baseline frames the paper's contribution： structured pruning trades post-prune accuracy for real speedup， 但needs intelligent structure selection (RASP) and RLVR recovery (GRPO) to close the accuracy gap。RASP+GRPO (64%) approaches unstructured (62%) while delivering 1.20x speedup——this is the practical value proposition。 Interesting：RASP+GRPO actually slightly beats unstructured+GRPO (64% vs 62%)。 这可能是noise但也可能说明structured pruning creates better GRPO training dynamics。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured 20% pruning保留much more accuracy post-prune (68% vs 30% RASP) 因为individual weight zeroing far less disruptive than removing entire channel groups。 Post-SFT仅微增到70%（already high baseline）。 Post-GRPO actually slightly lower (62%)——可能因为sparse weights的gradient flow 不如dense结构适合RLVR的exploration-exploitation dynamics。 关键：unstructured pruning无法获得real speedup (1.0x)因为sparse operations 在standard GPU hardware上不加速。这justifies structured pruning research。 Median档预期post_grpo 0.58-0.66，取0.62。 GRPO对unstructured model的recovery有限因为post-prune accuracy已经high (68%)， \\\"ceiling effect\\\"限制了further improvement，且部分accuracy可能lost to GRPO's exploration noise on already-functional model。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD Eval Contingency\",\n    \"description\": \"SFT-recovered Standard model (64% GSM8K) 在MATH-500和HumanEval上评估。 Check if 1%→64% SFT jump is genuine reasoning recovery vs GSM8K memorization。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_standard_math500\": 0.3,\n      \"sft_standard_humaneval\": 0.35,\n      \"sft_standard_gsm8k_ref\": 0.64,\n      \"sft_rasp_math500\": 0.28,\n      \"sft_rasp_humaneval\": 0.33,\n      \"sft_rasp_gsm8k_ref\": 0.57,\n      \"dense_math500_ref\": 0.52,\n      \"dense_humaneval_ref\": 0.58,\n      \"math500_retention_standard_sft\": 0.58,\n      \"humaneval_retention_standard_sft\": 0.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 14: SFT Recovery OOD Check\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"MATH-500\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Dense\",\n            \"79.0%\",\n            \"52.0%\",\n            \"58.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SFT-Standard\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"30.0%\",\n            \"35.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SFT-RASP\",\n            \"57.0%\",\n            \"28.0%\",\n            \"33.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRPO-RASP\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"38.0%\",\n            \"42.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GRPO-Standard\",\n            \"59.0%\",\n            \"33.0%\",\n            \"41.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT recovery不是memorization——OOD performance confirms genuine recovery。 但GRPO recovery consistently delivers higher OOD retention， especially on MATH-500 (38% vs 30% for best SFT)。 This adds to Claim 3：GRPO不仅在GSM8K上favor RASP， 在OOD上也delivers deeper、more generalizable recovery。\\n\\nStandard SFT 64% GSM8K的1%→64%跳跃确实suspicious——但SFT是supervised training， 能够快速恢复format和basic arithmetic。MATH-500上30% (vs dense 52%) 说明SFT recovery是genuine但partial——不仅是GSM8K pattern memorization， 因为MATH-500难度更高，30%仍代表real reasoning能力（random baseline ~5%）。 HumanEval 35%同样说明generalized recovery。 关键comparison：SFT-Standard MATH-500 (30%) vs GRPO-RASP MATH-500 (38%)—— GRPO recovery在OOD上更robust，支持\\\"RLVR enables deeper recovery\\\"的argument。 但SFT-Standard > SFT-RASP on MATH-500 (30% vs 28%)—— SFT recovery maintain Standard's advantage even OOD。Interaction story holds。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":872,"startLine":1,"totalLines":872}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Yqh9X4hhAsZCDbLS2cKc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight (Redundancy Paradox)\n9\tTraditional structured pruning selects structures to remove based on importance metrics alone (weight magnitude, gradient sensitivity). We show this misses a critical signal for RLVR recovery: **functional uniqueness**. Structures with high functional overlap (high CKA) can be safely pruned because RLVR redistributes their function across retained structures. Structures with low overlap are functionally irreplaceable — once removed, even RLVR cannot recreate their unique contribution. This creates a **Redundancy Paradox**: protecting functionally unique structures matters more for recovery than protecting high-importance structures.\n10\t\n11\tRASP exploits this via S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α: high overlap → low score → **pruned first**; low overlap → high score → **protected**. The result: RASP preferentially removes functionally redundant structures (whose function RLVR can recover) while Standard pruning may accidentally remove functionally unique structures that happen to have low importance scores. At 20% sparsity, this effect manifests entirely within MLP channel groups (0/112 attention GQA groups are pruned under either method; all 200 pruned structures are MLP groups), consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism (ICLR 2026).\n12\t\n13\t## Core Claims (3)\n14\t\n15\t1. **CKA-aware pruning preserves reasoning ability**: At matched sparsity and parameter count, RASP preserves significantly more post-prune reasoning accuracy than importance-only pruning (MVP evidence: 29% vs 1% GSM8K at 20% sparsity, p<0.0001), and this gap enables qualitatively different recovery outcomes (RASP-pruned models can be recovered via RLVR; standard-pruned models cannot).\n16\t\n17\t2. **Functional overlap predicts per-structure recoverability** *(scope: MLP channel groups at moderate sparsity)*: Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h) is a stronger predictor of post-recovery accuracy retention than standard importance metrics alone, within the MLP channel groups that are actually pruned at 20-25% sparsity. At these sparsity levels, attention GQA groups consistently rank above all MLP groups in the global importance list (0/112 pruned); the CKA signal's practical effect is selecting *which* MLP groups to prune (N=784, ~200 pruned). Validated via mixed-effects regression (layer as random effect) on MLP groups, controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. Cross-component (attention + MLP) validation requires higher sparsity (~40%+).\n18\t\n19\t3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning order**: The relative ranking of pruning strategies changes depending on recovery method (RLVR vs SFT). Structures expendable under RLVR recovery may be critical under SFT recovery, consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism — RLVR compresses incorrect paths (tolerates removal of overlapping structures) while SFT expands correct paths (needs preserved trajectory-encoding structures).\n20\t\n21\t## Story Spine\n22\t\n23\t- **Problem**: Structured pruning for reasoning LLMs optimizes for immediate post-pruning accuracy, treating subsequent recovery as independent. At moderate sparsity (20-35%), this disconnect can be catastrophic: standard importance-based pruning collapses reasoning ability to near-zero, making recovery impossible regardless of method. The choice of what to prune determines whether recovery can succeed at all.\n24\t\n25\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) shows RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression but uses standard pruning and tests only one ratio. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study reasoning-specific recovery. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration but has no recovery phase. No work studies how the pruning structure choice interacts with RLVR recovery quality, or whether optimal pruning differs for RLVR vs SFT recovery.\n26\t\n27\t- **Our framing**: We introduce Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP), reframing structural redundancy from a flaw to eliminate into a signal of RLVR recoverability. RASP scores structures by S(h) = I(h) × (1 - F(h))^α, protecting functionally unique reasoning scaffolding while allowing removal of structures whose function can be redistributed through RLVR. This connects to the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis at a new level: LTH asks \"which subnetwork trains well\" (binary); RASP asks \"which structures to remove so the remainder recovers well under a specific training paradigm\" (paradigm-conditioned trainability).\n28\t\n29\t- **Headline result template**: \"At 20% structured sparsity on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, RASP preserves 29% GSM8K accuracy (vs 1% for standard pruning), enabling RLVR recovery to X% while standard-pruned models remain unrecoverable. Per-structure CKA overlap explains Y% of variance in recovery outcomes (mixed-effects β = Z, p < 0.001).\"\n30\t\n31\t## Venue Fit\n32\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: natural fit for structured pruning + reasoning model recovery\n33\t- Reasoning model compression is timely (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, etc. driving demand)\n34\t- Empirical rigor + mechanistic analysis aligns with EMNLP's preference for thorough experimentation\n35\t\n36\t## Venue Fit Risks\n37\t- **\"Just another pruning metric\"**: Mitigate with Redundancy Paradox framing, LTH generalization (paradigm-conditioned trainability), and mechanistic analysis showing WHY it works\n38\t- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the most widely-used open reasoning model; multi-sparsity + multi-method comparison compensates\n39\t- **\"MPruner already uses CKA\"**: Different granularity (intra-layer per-head vs inter-layer), different objective (recoverability prediction vs redundancy removal), different domain (reasoning LLM vs CNN/general transformer)\n40\t- **\"Cross-component pruning not observed\"**: At 20-25% sparsity, only MLP groups are pruned (0 attention groups). Framework scores both types jointly, but global ranking at moderate sparsity naturally prioritizes MLP removal. Mitigate by: (1) honest description of actual pruning distribution, (2) noting the CKA signal still drives 29% vs 1% gap via MLP group reranking, (3) optionally test higher sparsity where attention groups enter pruning range\n41\t\n42\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n43\t\n44\t| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n45\t|---------|----------|----------------------|\n46\t| Incremental over importance-only pruning | 28pp post-prune gap is qualitative, not incremental; enables vs prevents recovery | exp-001, exp-002 |\n47\t| CKA overlap might correlate with simpler metrics | Scoring ablation: CKA vs magnitude/gradient/random | exp-007 |\n48\t| Single model generalization | Multi-sparsity (20%, 25%, 30%) + multi-method (Standard, GRASPrune, RASP) | exp-003, exp-005 |\n49\t| RLVR vs SFT claim needs controlled comparison | Same pruned models, same data budget, different recovery method | exp-006 |\n50\t| Statistical rigor of correlation claim | Mixed-effects regression with covariates on MLP groups (N=784, ~200 pruned) | exp-008 |\n51\t| Only MLP groups pruned at 20% sparsity | Honest description + CKA still drives 29% vs 1% via MLP reranking + optional higher sparsity test | experiments.tex |\n52\t| Recovery might just reflect post-prune accuracy | Include GRASPrune (different post-prune accuracy profile) to break correlation | exp-005 |\n53\t\n54\t## Key Differentiations\n55\t- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → RASP uses intra-layer CKA between individual heads for width pruning in reasoning LLMs, optimizing for post-recovery (not immediate) performance\n56\t- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: tests RLVR recovery with standard pruning → RASP optimizes the pruning decision FOR recovery\n57\t- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → RASP includes recovery-awareness in the pruning score\n58\t- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery study → GRASPrune is our primary baseline\n59\t- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → RASP optimizes pruning STRUCTURE (complementary)\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80acf845-bd40-40fe-a62c-7979cde6caad","uuid":"c8362ab2-eefc-40df-8b0d-b52280c66d18","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:41:50.062Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Insight (Redundancy Paradox)\nTraditional structured pruning selects structures to remove based on importance metrics alone (weight magnitude, gradient sensitivity). We show this misses a critical signal for RLVR recovery: **functional uniqueness**. Structures with high functional overlap (high CKA) can be safely pruned because RLVR redistributes their function across retained structures. Structures with low overlap are functionally irreplaceable — once removed, even RLVR cannot recreate their unique contribution. This creates a **Redundancy Paradox**: protecting functionally unique structures matters more for recovery than protecting high-importance structures.\n\nRASP exploits this via S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α: high overlap → low score → **pruned first**; low overlap → high score → **protected**. The result: RASP preferentially removes functionally redundant structures (whose function RLVR can recover) while Standard pruning may accidentally remove functionally unique structures that happen to have low importance scores. At 20% sparsity, this effect manifests entirely within MLP channel groups (0/112 attention GQA groups are pruned under either method; all 200 pruned structures are MLP groups), consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism (ICLR 2026).\n\n## Core Claims (3)\n\n1. **CKA-aware pruning preserves reasoning ability**: At matched sparsity and parameter count, RASP preserves significantly more post-prune reasoning accuracy than importance-only pruning (MVP evidence: 29% vs 1% GSM8K at 20% sparsity, p<0.0001), and this gap enables qualitatively different recovery outcomes (RASP-pruned models can be recovered via RLVR; standard-pruned models cannot).\n\n2. **Functional overlap predicts per-structure recoverability** *(scope: MLP channel groups at moderate sparsity)*: Per-structure CKA functional overlap F(h) is a stronger predictor of post-recovery accuracy retention than standard importance metrics alone, within the MLP channel groups that are actually pruned at 20-25% sparsity. At these sparsity levels, attention GQA groups consistently rank above all MLP groups in the global importance list (0/112 pruned); the CKA signal's practical effect is selecting *which* MLP groups to prune (N=784, ~200 pruned). Validated via mixed-effects regression (layer as random effect) on MLP groups, controlling for weight norm, gradient importance, and activation magnitude. Cross-component (attention + MLP) validation requires higher sparsity (~40%+).\n\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning order**: The relative ranking of pruning strategies changes depending on recovery method (RLVR vs SFT). Structures expendable under RLVR recovery may be critical under SFT recovery, consistent with the \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" mechanism — RLVR compresses incorrect paths (tolerates removal of overlapping structures) while SFT expands correct paths (needs preserved trajectory-encoding structures).\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Structured pruning for reasoning LLMs optimizes for immediate post-pruning accuracy, treating subsequent recovery as independent. At moderate sparsity (20-35%), this disconnect can be catastrophic: standard importance-based pruning collapses reasoning ability to near-zero, making recovery impossible regardless of method. The choice of what to prune determines whether recovery can succeed at all.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) shows RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression but uses standard pruning and tests only one ratio. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study reasoning-specific recovery. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration but has no recovery phase. No work studies how the pruning structure choice interacts with RLVR recovery quality, or whether optimal pruning differs for RLVR vs SFT recovery.\n\n- **Our framing**: We introduce Recovery-Aware Structured Pruning (RASP), reframing structural redundancy from a flaw to eliminate into a signal of RLVR recoverability. RASP scores structures by S(h) = I(h) × (1 - F(h))^α, protecting functionally unique reasoning scaffolding while allowing removal of structures whose function can be redistributed through RLVR. This connects to the Lottery Ticket Hypothesis at a new level: LTH asks \"which subnetwork trains well\" (binary); RASP asks \"which structures to remove so the remainder recovers well under a specific training paradigm\" (paradigm-conditioned trainability).\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"At 20% structured sparsity on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, RASP preserves 29% GSM8K accuracy (vs 1% for standard pruning), enabling RLVR recovery to X% while standard-pruned models remain unrecoverable. Per-structure CKA overlap explains Y% of variance in recovery outcomes (mixed-effects β = Z, p < 0.001).\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: natural fit for structured pruning + reasoning model recovery\n- Reasoning model compression is timely (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, etc. driving demand)\n- Empirical rigor + mechanistic analysis aligns with EMNLP's preference for thorough experimentation\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **\"Just another pruning metric\"**: Mitigate with Redundancy Paradox framing, LTH generalization (paradigm-conditioned trainability), and mechanistic analysis showing WHY it works\n- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the most widely-used open reasoning model; multi-sparsity + multi-method comparison compensates\n- **\"MPruner already uses CKA\"**: Different granularity (intra-layer per-head vs inter-layer), different objective (recoverability prediction vs redundancy removal), different domain (reasoning LLM vs CNN/general transformer)\n- **\"Cross-component pruning not observed\"**: At 20-25% sparsity, only MLP groups are pruned (0 attention groups). Framework scores both types jointly, but global ranking at moderate sparsity naturally prioritizes MLP removal. Mitigate by: (1) honest description of actual pruning distribution, (2) noting the CKA signal still drives 29% vs 1% gap via MLP group reranking, (3) optionally test higher sparsity where attention groups enter pruning range\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\n| Incremental over importance-only pruning | 28pp post-prune gap is qualitative, not incremental; enables vs prevents recovery | exp-001, exp-002 |\n| CKA overlap might correlate with simpler metrics | Scoring ablation: CKA vs magnitude/gradient/random | exp-007 |\n| Single model generalization | Multi-sparsity (20%, 25%, 30%) + multi-method (Standard, GRASPrune, RASP) | exp-003, exp-005 |\n| RLVR vs SFT claim needs controlled comparison | Same pruned models, same data budget, different recovery method | exp-006 |\n| Statistical rigor of correlation claim | Mixed-effects regression with covariates on MLP groups (N=784, ~200 pruned) | exp-008 |\n| Only MLP groups pruned at 20% sparsity | Honest description + CKA still drives 29% vs 1% via MLP reranking + optional higher sparsity test | experiments.tex |\n| Recovery might just reflect post-prune accuracy | Include GRASPrune (different post-prune accuracy profile) to break correlation | exp-005 |\n\n## Key Differentiations\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → RASP uses intra-layer CKA between individual heads for width pruning in reasoning LLMs, optimizing for post-recovery (not immediate) performance\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: tests RLVR recovery with standard pruning → RASP optimizes the pruning decision FOR recovery\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → RASP includes recovery-awareness in the pruning score\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery study → GRASPrune is our primary baseline\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → RASP optimizes pruning STRUCTURE (complementary)\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}}}
